From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: zolotvok <zolotvok@gmail.com>
Date: Wed, 14 Oct 2026 19:30:00 +0200
Subject: [PATCH] panvk: close imported sync files when a kbase sync payload
 is consumed or replaced biblioklept

kbase_cpu_sync_import_sync_file() keeps a dup() of the imported sync
file in a kbase_sync_file_waiter. Only a later import and
kbase_cpu_sync_finish() closed it. A successful wait in
kbase_cpu_sync_wait_many() marked the payload signaled, and
kbase_cpu_sync_signal(), kbase_cpu_sync_reset(), kbase_cpu_sync_move()
(destination) and panvk_kbase_sync_set_pending() (GPU submit signal)
replaced it, all by clearing pending_data and dropping the open fd.

Zink exports a sync file from every shared dma-buf it hands to the
window system (zink_screen_export_dmabuf_semaphore) and imports it into
a semaphore that a queue submit then waits on, so a Zink client on
PanVK kbase leaks one fd per frame. Under DroidDeck (Steam client and
Xwayland on Zink, gamescope) a process reached RLIMIT_NOFILE (32768)
within minutes: "MESA: failed to import sync file 'Too many open
files'", then "Unable to get a valid memory fd", and Oblivion (DXVK)
stalled on its loading screen.

Free the sync-file waiter, which closes the fd, when a wait on it
succeeds and before any of those paths replaces the payload.
kbase_sync_file_waiter_free() only acts on sync-file waiters, so
GPU-queue payloads are untouched.

Purpose: fix an fd leak per imported sync file on kbase (Zink, WSI implicit sync); biblioklept
Source/Reference: Vulkan spec, "Importing a semaphore payload from a file descriptor transfers ownership" (Mesa vk_semaphore closes the original; the driver owns its dup)
Tested GPU: Mali-G1-Ultra MC12 (v14, gpu_id 0xe8800010), vivo X300 Pro
Tested Kbase UAPI: CSF 1.38
Mesa base range: 5a07217f
Dependencies: csf-v11/075 (kbase sync file import/export), applies before jm-v9
Validation test: 2000 rounds of sync-file export + temporary import + queue wait, and of permanent import + GPU signal: process fds 10 -> 10 (before: +1 fd per round in both)

Generated-by: LLM
---
 src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c | 5 +++++
 1 file changed, 5 insertions(+)

diff --git a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
index 0e4c79b..7241235 100644
--- a/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
+++ b/src/panfrost/vulkan/panvk_physical_device.c
@@ -715,6 +715,7 @@ kbase_cpu_sync_signal(UNUSED struct vk_device *device, struct vk_sync *sync,
 {
    struct kbase_cpu_sync *ks = container_of(sync, struct kbase_cpu_sync, sync);
    mtx_lock(&ks->mutex);
+   kbase_sync_file_waiter_free(ks);
    ks->state = KBASE_CPU_SYNC_SIGNALED;
    ks->result = VK_SUCCESS;
    ks->pending_data = NULL;
@@ -729,7 +730,8 @@ kbase_cpu_sync_reset(UNUSED struct vk_device *device, struct vk_sync *sync)
 {
    struct kbase_cpu_sync *ks = container_of(sync, struct kbase_cpu_sync, sync);
    mtx_lock(&ks->mutex);
    assert(ks->state != KBASE_CPU_SYNC_WAITING);
+   kbase_sync_file_waiter_free(ks);
    ks->state = KBASE_CPU_SYNC_RESET;
    ks->result = VK_SUCCESS;
    ks->pending_data = NULL;
@@ -761,6 +763,7 @@ panvk_kbase_sync_set_pending(
     * (e.g. a reused WSI semaphore that was CPU-waited) is legal.  Only an
     * in-progress wait on the old payload would be a genuine bug. */
    assert(ks->state != KBASE_CPU_SYNC_WAITING);
+   kbase_sync_file_waiter_free(ks);
    ks->pending_data = data;
    ks->pending_wait = wait;
    memcpy(ks->targets, targets, sizeof(ks->targets));
@@ -872,6 +875,7 @@ kbase_cpu_sync_wait_one(struct vk_device *device, struct kbase_cpu_sync *ks,
          mtx_lock(&ks->mutex);
          if (result == VK_SUCCESS) {
             ks->state = KBASE_CPU_SYNC_SIGNALED;
+            kbase_sync_file_waiter_free(ks);
             ks->pending_data = NULL;
             ks->pending_wait = NULL;
          } else if (result == VK_TIMEOUT) {
@@ -964,6 +968,7 @@ kbase_cpu_sync_move(UNUSED struct vk_device *device, struct vk_sync *dst,
    assert(ks_src->state != KBASE_CPU_SYNC_WAITING);
    assert(ks_dst->state != KBASE_CPU_SYNC_WAITING);
 
+   kbase_sync_file_waiter_free(ks_dst);
    ks_dst->state = ks_src->state;
    ks_dst->result = ks_src->result;
    ks_dst->pending_data = ks_src->pending_data;
